Source: zionos-apps
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: ZionOS Developers <zionos-devel@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake (>= 3.25), ninja-build,
 qt6-base-dev, qt6-tools-dev, qt6-tools-dev-tools, qt6-l10n-tools,
 qtkeychain-qt6-dev, libgl1-mesa-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: zionos-apps-common
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, zionos-artwork
Description: ZionOS applications - translations
 Hebrew translations shared by the ZionOS Welcome, Settings and Assistant
 applications. English is built in.

Package: zionos-welcome
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, zionos-apps-common (= ${source:Version}),
 zionos-settings (= ${binary:Version}), qt6-translations-l10n
Description: ZionOS welcome application
 First-run window of ZionOS: language choice (English or Hebrew) and
 shortcuts to installing the system, software, settings and the assistant.

Package: zionos-settings
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, zionos-apps-common (= ${source:Version}),
 qt6-translations-l10n
Recommends: systemsettings, plasma-discover
Suggests: flatpak
Description: ZionOS settings and "About ZionOS"
 ZionOS-specific settings: display language, English/Hebrew keyboard layouts
 and switching shortcut, assistant providers and API keys, optional Flatpak
 repository, and system information. Other settings are delegated to KDE
 System Settings.

Package: zionos-assistant
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, zionos-apps-common (= ${source:Version}),
 ca-certificates, qt6-translations-l10n
Recommends: kwalletmanager, libpam-kwallet5
Description: ZionOS desktop AI assistant
 Optional desktop assistant that talks to the OpenAI or Anthropic API with a
 key supplied by the user. Keys are kept in the desktop keyring, replies are
 streamed, conversation history stays on the local computer, and suggested
 commands are only displayed - never executed.
 .
 The assistant is not required for any other part of ZionOS.
